Low-Mach damping does nothing to the energy row because it is a fourth
difference of the \emph{velocity} and does not touch the pressure
truncation error. Three seeds whose base velocities differ by a factor
$10^{4}$ reach one solution ($\rho$ to $3.4\times10^{-10}$, $v$ to
$2.5\times10^{-8}$, $\dot M$ to seven digits), which is what makes the
campaign's answers independent of which solved state seeded them.

\subsection{The secondary-ionization coupling, applied from the first evaluation}

\texttt{Secondary\_ionization} defaults to \texttt{STAGED}, which arms the
Shull \& van Steenberg (1985) channel only when a march first converges.
The stationary route takes no time step, so a state solved under the default
is written with the coupling off while the post-processing pass --- which
applies it unconditionally, and is where every number quoted here comes from
--- reports the same wind with it on. MEASURED on the $K_{zz} = 10^{9}$,
$\mathrm{He/H} = 1.6261$ case: $\log_{10}\dot M = 8.29$ under the default
against $7.87$ with \texttt{Secondary\_ionization:\ Immediate}, and
$n(\mathrm{He}\,2\,^3S)$ differs by $74$ per cent beyond $1.5\,R_p$, which is
where the line forms. Every case of the campaign carries the key.

\subsection{The C, N and O line cooling at the local electron density}
\label{sec:cnocooling}

Six coolants the photochemical column brings into the base ---
C\,\textsc{i}, C\,\textsc{ii}, N\,\textsc{i}, N\,\textsc{ii}, O\,\textsc{i}
and O\,\textsc{ii} --- were evaluated in the coronal limit, that is above
the critical density of the levels they excite. Against the CHIANTI
statistical equilibrium of the same ion, the coefficient the cooling
assembly took stood at $0.02$ to $5.4\times10^{4}$ times the right value
over the wind-relevant domain; the replacement, a density-resolved table
read at the cell's own electron density, stands at $0.969$ to $1.009$ at
every point of a $7\times6$ grid spanning $1000$ to $20\,000$\,K and
$10^{4}$ to $10^{9}$\,cm$^{-3}$ (item L6b). A second defect was found in the
closed-form fits those six terms used and is removed from the production
path with them: the fits were built from the CHIANTI \texttt{.scups}
\emph{theoretical} transition energies while the level populations that
decide the emission use the \emph{observed} level energies, and the two
differ by up to $14$ per cent in $\Delta E$ for the O\,\textsc{ii}
$^4S^{\circ}$--$^2D^{\circ}$ excitation, which at $2000$\,K is a factor $14$
in $\exp(-\Delta E/kT)$.

This is the change that reshaped the solved-column branch of this memo. The
metal content of the base is no longer a thermostat: MEASURED at
$\mathrm{He/H} = 2.13$ over the scalar base, adding the column's C, N and O
reservoirs moves $T_{\max}$ from $5694$ to $5537$\,K and the red-pair
equivalent width from $1.3934$ to $1.3917$\,\%\,\AA{}.

\subsection{The outer boundary}

The LHS\,1140\,b wind is subsonic at $30\,R_p$, so the free-outflow
continuation of the outer ghost is not a passive extrapolation: one
characteristic points inward and the ghost rule \emph{is} the external
condition. Solving the same case on $45$ and $60\,R_p$ domains settles what
that costs (item L8). The wind is transonic, with its critical point at
$40.06$ and $40.08\,R_p$ in the two extended runs, and once the boundary is
outside that point the two solutions agree with each other to better than
$0.1$ per cent everywhere. The $30\,R_p$ answer survives where it is used
and fails where it is not: $\log_{10}\dot M = 7.8737$, $7.8740$, $7.8735$ at
$30$, $45$ and $60\,R_p$ and the He\,\textsc{i} $10830$ equivalent width
within $1.7$ per cent, against $25$ per cent in temperature, $29$ in density
and $22$ in velocity at $28\,R_p$. \emph{No profile above about $10\,R_p$ is
quoted from these runs.} The exobase of the extended solutions sits at
$29.0\,R_p$, below the critical point, so the continuum model fixes its own
topology in gas it cannot describe; the mass-flux insensitivity is a
statement about the discrete problem and not a physical validation.

\subsection{The composition above 4\,$R_p$}
\label{sec:frozencomp}

The wind is solved with a photoionization-equilibrium composition, and above
about $4\,R_p$ that composition is not the one the gas carries. Over a flow
time $r/v$ the hydrogen recombines $1.7$ times at $2\,R_p$ and
$5\times10^{-3}$ times at $29\,R_p$, and is photoionized $7\times10^{-2}$
and $10^{-2}$ times at the same radii (item L10): the ionization state is
frozen into the parcel and carried outward. The equilibrium neutral fraction
falls from $0.963$ at $2\,R_p$ to $0.346$ at $29\,R_p$ while the
advection-corrected one goes from $0.974$ to $0.941$, and the photoheating
that follows the neutral density stands a factor $5.9$ apart at $44\,R_p$.
The consequence for the line is not a correction but a choice of file: the
He\,\textsc{i} $10830$ equivalent width read from the solution's own
composition is $15.5116$\,\%\,\AA{} against $1.1702$ from the
advection-corrected one, a factor $13.3$, while feeding the transit tool the
solution's \emph{temperature} with the corrected composition moves it by
$0.15$ per cent (item L12a). The line is a statement about the composition
and about almost nothing else in those two files, and every line number here
is read from the \texttt{\_adv} profiles. Carrying $x(\mathrm{H\,II})$,
$x(\mathrm{He\,II})$ and $x(\mathrm{He\,III})$ as transported fractions per
element nucleus is designed (item L12a) and not implemented.

One defect was found and fixed on the way: the advection correction
discarded MINPACK roots returned with \texttt{info} $= 4$ even where the
iterate satisfied the energy equation to $10^{-17}$ of the largest term the
equation holds, and because the correction is an upwind recursion the
discard restarted the temperature profile at every row above it. With the
roots accepted by their residual the $45$ and $60\,R_p$ corrected
temperatures agree to $0.19$ per cent, which is the $0.28$ per cent at which
the two \emph{solutions} agree.

\subsection{The convergence procedure at low XUV}

Five cases of the XUV grid did not certify on the first campaign, and the
reason is in the outer loop rather than in the wind (item L14). The
alternation is ``solve the wind at fixed composition, relax the composition
at fixed wind''. Its own error is the undamped distance the element
relaxation returns, which the under-relaxation contracts by $1-\omega$ per
pass; the progress control reads a different quantity, the distance of the
state from certification, and where \emph{that} fails to fall it halves
$\omega$ --- taking the contraction from $2.00$ to $1.14$ per pass --- and
after three such passes ends the loop. On these cases the two quantities
disagree from the first pass: the composition distance falls every pass
while the gated elemental He/H row rises. The certified case at $0.30$ of
the same spectrum is the control: it entered at the same composition
distance, its gated row also failed to fall over its first pass, and it
