      grid still stands four times above the limit at its faintest solved
      point, $0.20$, and the three fainter points are pending.
\item \textbf{Not verified: the second-chemistry-code cross-check.} VULCAN
      did not converge on this cold helium-rich column, its convergence
      measure rose against the criterion with the timestep pinned, the
      limiting cell being H$_2$O at the cold trap, so no composition from
      a second code, and no cross-code spread, is quoted
      (Sect.~\ref{sec:closure}).
\item \textbf{Not solved: the molecular lower boundary.} Three groups of
      the model tree solve the molecular layer in EXHALE itself rather than
      taking it from the column, and none of them has a working recipe: a
      cold march stops on the chemical equilibrium of the cells below the
      base face, and the restart contract refuses an atomic state as a seed
      because the two carry different unknowns (\texttt{MODELS.md} Sect.~6).
      They are recorded as not solved, not as a result.
\end{itemize}

\noindent Four axes have now been walked: the assumed XUV spectrum, the
mixing assumption with its eddy coefficient, composition itself, and what is
placed at the lower boundary. Each separates the two questions rather than
answering them together. Every one of them moves the composition the
equivalent width implies, two of them by a large factor; none of them moves
the width. What is left as a possible source of the missing
$22$\,km\,s$^{-1}$ is therefore what it was: velocity fields that are
three-dimensional, or heating a 1D hydrodynamic energy equation does not
carry. The adiabatic-cooling metastable bump, the one candidate that would
have needed no free parameter, has been looked for on both spectra and does
not supply it for this host (Sect.~\ref{sec:bump}).

